<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Universal category — every unique melee weapon lists it. Carries Odyssey's six generic
       ported traits (cosmetic / value / weight; no on-hit effect): Ornamental, Ugly, Lightweight,
       Cumbersome, plus the Gold/Jade inlays. Includes UMW_Lightweight, the universal alone-able
       trait whose adjectives guarantee every weapon can be named.

       These six are INTENTIONAL self-contained ports — do NOT "DRY" them into XML inheritance
       (ParentName) from Odyssey's trait defs. Two hard reasons:
         1. Odyssey's trait defs carry no Name=, so ParentName can't target them without first
            patching one on (à la AddNameToBaseMeleeWeapons) — a hard load-order dependency on
            paid-DLC internals. A future Odyssey restructure then means "could not find parent node"
            → the trait fails to load → it drops out of UMW_Melee → and if that leaves a category
            with no alone-able adjective-bearing trait, weapon generation THROWS.
         2. No DRY win anyway: statOffsets/statFactors merge by element name (Verse.XmlInheritance.
            RecursiveNodeCopyOverwriteElements), so an inherited RangedWeapon_* stat can't be removed
            by override — only Inherit="False" drops it, which means restating the whole block.
       Two flavours, per file:
         • Re-pointed to melee stats — Ornamental, Lightweight, Cumbersome: Odyssey drives
           ranged-only stats (RangedWeapon_DamageMultiplier / _WarmupMultiplier) that are inert on
           melee, so these were redesigned onto MeleeWeapon_* stats. Each file notes its deltas inline.
         • Verbatim-equivalent — Ugly, Gold/Jade inlay: touch only category-agnostic stats
           (Beauty / MarketValue / forcedColor), so their values match Odyssey 1:1.

       Beyond the six ports the category carries our own universal traits: UMW_BloodStained (gory
       body tint + on-hit dread), the body-colour finishes UMW_Carbonized (durability and value traded
       for a small damage/AP gain) and
       UMW_Enameled (beauty), and UMW_Storied (mood passive + the Rallying Cry ability). Token
       registry for the tokens rooted here (tokens are global across categories):
         • "Color" (colour-one accent, red mask): Gold/Jade inlays; cross-category members
           Envenomed (Pointed) and ZeusHeaded (Blunt) force colour-one tints.
         • "BodyColor" (colour-two body, green mask — replaces the stuff tint): BloodStained,
           Carbonized, Enameled; cross-category members Monomolecular and PlasmaCored (Bladed).
         • "Appearance" (a weapon gets one look): Ornamental, Ugly, BloodStained, Carbonized,
           Enameled.
         • "Weight": Lightweight, Cumbersome.
         • "Ability" (one active/gizmo per weapon): Storied; cross-category member Piledriver
           (Blunt). -->
  <WeaponCategoryDef>
    <defName>UMW_Melee</defName>
    <label>melee</label>
  </WeaponCategoryDef>

</Defs>
